module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TensorPullbackAdjunction
public import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Module
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Cotangent
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.ModulePullbackAffineSections
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.ClosedImmersion
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Quotient

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

attribute [local instance] RingHomInvPair.of_ringEquiv RingHomInvPair.of_ringEquiv_symm

/-- The affine conormal linear equivalence and its compatibility with the adjunction unit.
Source: Stacks Project, Morphisms, Lemma 01R3 (2), together with Schemes, Tag 01I9
and Algebra, Tag 00DF.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-affine-conormal-sections-existence)

Proof: Put A = Γ(X,U) and V = i⁻¹U. A closed immersion is affine and its section
map ρ : A → Γ(Z,V) is surjective. Thus V is affine and, in the coordinates r,
Γ(Z,V) is R/I. The inclusion of i.ker.toModules is injective on sections and
its range on U is ker ρ, by range_toModulesι_app and ideal_ker. Consequently it
identifies Γ(i.ker.toModules,U) with I semilinearly along r; in particular the
section representing a is unique. This ideal module is quasi-coherent: it is
the kernel of O_X → (i.ker.subschemeι)_* O_{V(i.ker)}, and closed-immersion
pushforward and kernels preserve quasi-coherence.

Apply exists_tensorPullback_affine_sections to i, U, V and this ideal module.
Its bijective comparison sends s ⊗ b to b times the adjunction-unit section of s.
Transport along r and the quotient-ring identification above to obtain an
R-linear isomorphism I ⊗[R] (R/I) → Γ(i* i.ker.toModules,V).
The tensor swap followed by TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul identifies
the source with I/(I • ⊤), which is I.Cotangent: I • ⊤ as a submodule of I is
generated by the products of two elements of I. The inverse of this quotient
tensor equivalence sends the class of a to a ⊗ 1.

Compose these equivalences and restore the A-action through r to obtain the
stated semilinear e. Sections of pushforward on U are sections on V with
scalars restricted through ρ. The pure-tensor formula at b = 1 gives precisely
the displayed equality for the unique s representing a. No choice of section
or of quotient-ring coordinates affects this equality, since the maps are
specified on the generating classes of the elements of I. -/
theorem affine_conormal_sections_existence {X Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X)
    [IsClosedImmersion i] :
      ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (R : Type v) [CommRing R]
        (r : R ≃+* Γ(X, U.1)) (I : Ideal R),
        I = RingHom.ker ((i.app U.1).hom.comp (r : R →+* Γ(X, U.1))) →
        ∃ e : LinearEquiv (r : R →+* Γ(X, U.1))
            (σ' := (r.symm : Γ(X, U.1) →+* R)) I.Cotangent
            Γ((pushforward i).obj ((tensorPullback i).obj i.ker.toModules), U.1),
          ∀ (a : I) (s : Γ(i.ker.toModules, U.1)),
            i.ker.toModulesι.app U.1 s = r (a : R) →
            e (I.toCotangent a) =
              ((Classical.choose (exists_tensorPullbackAdjunction i)).unit.app
                i.ker.toModules).app U.1 s := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
